    Bug 2033503 - Fix intermittent failures in browser_subscribe.js by awaiting tree row clicks. r=tobyp


    The test frequently failed in `testNNTPSubscribe` because the test
    runner advanced to the assertions before the web component's microtask
    had finished updating the `TreeDataRow` checked properties.

    This patch stabilizes the test interactions by making the `clickTreeRow`
    helper asynchronous:
    1. It introduces a double `requestAnimationFrame` yield to ensure fully
       flushed layout changes before calculating synthetic click coordinates.
    2. It yields to the event loop via `setTimeout(0)` after dispatching the
       click, allowing the component's state to settle. All invocations of
       `clickTreeRow` have been updated to `await` this resolution.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D296992

